// Payments: the domain that refuses to mount, and the reason slicing matters.
//
// initiate_payment is annotated the way a bank actually needs it: destructive,
// irreversible, external, gated on a human grant, and written to an audit
// stream that must succeed before the money moves. Every one of those is true
// of the tool. None of them is implemented by a garmd with no GrantVerifier
// and no audit Sink — so that garmd REFUSES TO START rather than serve an
// irreversible payment ungated.
//
// Do not weaken these annotations to make the build go green. A payment tool
// that mounts with less supervision than its schema claims is worse than one
// that will not mount, because the declaration reads as protection to everyone
// who reviews it. The refusal is the feature.
//
// It is also the demonstration of why a bank cannot have ONE catalogue. Build
// this tree into a single artifact and nothing in the bank serves, because one
// domain declared supervision this deployment cannot apply. Build it per
// domain and accounts, cards and screening come up while payments stays down
// until its dependencies exist. See README.md.

